AcquisitionMethod: data-dependent acquisition mode
Age: 8-12 weeks
AlkylationReagent: iodoacetamide
CleavageAgent: trypsin
Depletion: multiple affinity removal system (MARS; Agilent)
DevelopmentalStage: pregnant
DevelopmentalStage: term delivery (>37 weeks)
DevelopmentalStage: E15.5-E17.5
DevelopmentalStage: E16.5-E18.5
EnrichmentMethod: SNA-I lectin chromatography
FactorValue: non-pregnant
FactorValue: pregnant
FactorValue: virgin
FactorValue: xmOVA-pregnant
FactorValue: pregnant women
FlowRateChromatogram: 300 nl min-1
FractionIdentifier: The flow-through fractions
FractionIdentifier: Eluates
FragmentationMethod: collision-induced dissociation
GradientTime: a linear gradient of 3-40% B for 105 min
Instrument: TripleTOF 6600 mass spectrometer (SCIEX)
IonizationType: electrospray ionization
MaterialType: biofluid
NumberOfBiologicalReplicates: 3
Organism: humans
Organism: mice
OrganismPart: Human plasma
OrganismPart: Mouse plasma
PooledSample: pooled
ReductionReagent: 10 mM TCEP
SamplingTime: Plasma from pregnant women was collected at the time of term delivery (>37 weeks).
Separation: trap column (NanoLC Trap ChromXP, 350 mum i.d. x 0.5 mm, 3-mum particle size, 120 Aa pore size)
Separation: ChromXP C18 column (75 mum i.d. x 15 cm, 3-mum particle size, 120 Aa pore size)
